	'k73a2ed80' => 'How does the theme of voluntary solitude develop across the twenty-one essays?',
	'k73f1322c' => 'Hsu\'s publishing history traces a steady dedication to independent small-press literature. In 2014, she published her first essay in a small-press zine, establishing her interest in short personal essays. In 2018, Fumi Press published her debut collection, Window Seat. Beginning in 2022, Hsu committed to writing at the same café table every morning, producing the essays that culminated in her 2027 collection Small Hours. She drafts entirely by hand using a fountain pen and lined notebooks, focusing on the immediate sensory details of her surroundings.',
	'k768e23b8' => 'The audiobook edition of Small Hours is narrated directly by the author, Clara Hsu, providing an authentic interpretation of her prose rhythms. Recorded in a quiet studio in Taipei, the complete unabridged reading has a total duration of 6 hours and 40 minutes. The audiobook is priced at USD 18 and will be delivered on 18 March 2027 as high-bitrate, DRM-free audio files.',
	'k77d5e42c' => 'The light enters Da\'an District along the wet asphalt before the first scooter passes. At seven in the morning, the corner table is already wiped down, cool to the palm, holding a circle of grey sky from the high eastern window.',
