	'k7e99ea71' => 'Everything that matters in an essay begins as something too ordinary to mention. A cup of black coffee cooling beside an open notebook, the sound of spoons against porcelain, the unfamiliar quiet of a capital city before its machinery turns over. In these small hours, before the day demands an account of itself, the world presents its surfaces without insistence.',
