	'kab1d0d75' => '248 pages, 14 × 21 cm, publication date 18 March 2027',
	'kabb8c44b' => 'You can contact Fumi Press by emailing hello@fumipress.example. Our studio in Da\'an District, Taipei operates Monday through Friday from 10:00 to 18:00 GMT+8. Our team reads every message and responds within two working days. For international rights, translation licensing, and media interview requests, our rights manager Elena Brandt handles inquiries directly from our Berlin press office.',
	'kae6cde26' => 'Limited to 1,500 numbered copies, 248 pages, 14 × 21 cm, ships 11 March 2027',
	'kaec76f4f' => 'Seven ways to hold it',
	'kaf2a4d28' => 'Frequently asked questions',
	'kaf619b82' => 'Rafael Ortiz · Teacher &amp; Book-Club Host',
	'kb1637ed3' => 'USD 34',
	'kb1a8657c' => 'What significance does the handwritten draft hold in a modern metropolis?',
	'kb1ea45b3' => 'Clara Hsu is an essayist based in Taipei whose writing examines ordinary spaces, urban solitude, and morning routines. Her second collection, Small Hours, is published by Fumi Press.',
	'kb29f82b4' => 'Seats',
	'kb357b524' => 'Email address',
	'kb36d2184' => 'Specifications',
	'kb3c01a08' => 'Studio notes',
	'kb5d20c81' => 'Launch Bundles and Support Contacts',
	'kba154898' => 'Biographical Note',
	'kbcb42cd5' => 'Orders ship worldwide from Taipei using tracked postal and courier services. Delivery typically takes between 5 and 12 working days depending on destination customs clearance. Shipping rates are calculated at checkout based on destination country and parcel weight. Pre-ordered copies ship on 11 March 2027 so that readers receive their books as close as possible to the official 18 March 2027 publication date.',
	'kbe791aff' => 'The chair is bentwood, polished smooth at the armrests by years of coats and elbows. By six in the morning, the streetlamps along the avenue are still casting amber circles on the pavement, but the bakery across the lane has already switched on its fluorescent tubes. I sit here before the milk delivery arrives, watching the steam rise from my first cup of black coffee. The table itself is round, small enough that my notebook and saucer occupy almost the entire marble surface.',
	'kbee0a8cf' => 'Nothing here yet.',
	'kbf5cda6f' => 'Pre-order received',
	'kc050e994' => '10 March 2027',
	'kc15750b0' => 'Bicycle Bells',
	'kc1df1da7' => 'Contents',
	'kc38fea0a' => 'To support reading groups, Fumi Press offers a complete Book-club pack for USD 110. This package includes six paperback copies of Small Hours—available in English or Traditional Chinese—along with our printed reading guide. The guide outlines a suggested three-session discussion schedule, dividing the twenty-one essays into manageable thematic units. It also includes background notes from editor Tomas Reyes on the four-year drafting process and contextual observations regarding the neighborhoods of Taipei.',
	'kc3b28d07' => 'Hanna Weber · Reader',
	'kc4ffb8fa' => 'Conversation with Tomas Reyes',
	'kc5f29bb3' => 'Privacy',
	'kc62cf638' => 'This essay opens the twenty-one pieces collected in Small Hours, which spans 248 pages in a 14 × 21 cm format. The complete volume will be published on 18 March 2027 in both English and Traditional Chinese editions. Readers wishing to secure the signed first printing of 1,500 numbered hardcover copies can pre-order through our editions page before orders close on 10 March 2027. All pre-ordered copies ship directly from Taipei on 11 March 2027.',
	'kc7ed8cb1' => 'Twenty-one small hours, one table, the city going by.',
	'kc890bc11' => 'When will Small Hours be published and when do pre-orders ship?',
	'kc97432a8' => 'Your pre-order is registered.',
	'kca67b723' => 'How do weather and rain shift the emotional tone of Part Three?',
	'kcccd2112' => 'I have kept this morning routine since 2022, sitting at the exact same corner table with a fountain pen and a lined notebook. One does not need extraordinary events to understand a neighborhood; one only needs to remain in place long enough for the ordinary to reveal its pattern. The sunlight arrives around seven, cutting an ivory diagonal across the paper and illuminating the dust motes suspended in the quiet room. By the time the second pot of coffee brews, the first page is finished.',
	'kcce0a6fe' => 'What does the collection suggest about finding stillness in daily life?',
	'kccf214b8' => 'Da&#8217;an District, early morning.',
	'kcf603677' => 'Book clubs',
	'kd18844c5' => 'Noor Haddad, book design and cover typography',
	'kd1c279b5' => 'Audiobook read by the author (6 h 40 min)',
	'kd2acf3c6' => 'Working method',
	'kd2b605d7' => 'Tomas Reyes',
	'kd2e8cf62' => 'What is included in the Book-club pack and printed reading guide?',
	'kd52745a3' => 'The Launch bundle is priced at USD 58 and includes three items: a signed and numbered hardcover copy of Small Hours, a custom blank canvas tote bag, and one reserved seat at a launch reading of your choice. Bundle holders receive an email confirmation two weeks before their selected city\'s event date with check-in instructions. Event seats are available in Taipei, Tokyo, Paris, or Berlin.',
	'kd5b4031f' => '“A rare collection that earns its quietness. Every sentence feels weighed, cut, and placed with complete care.”',
	'kd5ea2133' => 'For booksellers, reviewers and journalists',
	'kd658dee5' => 'See the book-club pack →',
	'kd6d2209b' => 'Reading + translator Q&amp;A',
	'kd748a574' => 'Reading + book-club evening with Hanna Weber',
	'kd8b9045c' => 'Data Retention and Reader Rights',
	'kd8cd25d4' => 'Join Clara Hsu for a four-city international reading tour celebrating the release of Small Hours. Admission to all four events is free, with strictly sixty seats available per venue upon advance reservation.',
	'kdae423b7' => 'Our digital press kit for Small Hours: Essays from a Corner Table contains complete promotional materials for literary coverage. Assets include Clara Hsu\'s author biography, high-resolution author portraits and documentary book images photographed by Jun Park, cover typography files designed by Noor Haddad, sample essays, and a bibliographic data sheet. Review copies and excerpt permissions may be requested by writing to hello@fumipress.example.',
	'kdbee4b77' => 'Pre-ordering',
	'kdc2a8352' => '19:30 · Reading and translator Q&amp;A',
	'kde08ef55' => 'Pre-order',
	'kdeefd133' => 'Yes, the Ebook edition is priced at USD 12 and comes as a universal, DRM-free EPUB file compatible with all standard e-readers, tablets, and reading applications. Uniquely, the digital purchase includes complete text files for both the English and Traditional Chinese editions, allowing bilingual readers to compare translations side by side. Download links are distributed via email on publication day, 18 March 2027.',
	'kdf1f8e49' => 'Doors open thirty minutes prior to each reading at 19:00 local time, and guests are kindly asked to take their seats by 19:25. All four selected venues—The Corner Room in Taipei, Annex Reading Room in Tokyo, Librairie du Quai Bas in Paris, and Lesesaal Nord in Berlin—offer step-free street access and accessible restroom facilities. Readings will last approximately forty-five minutes, followed by audience questions, author signing, and informal conversation.',
	'kdfa00bf6' => '1,500 numbered hardcover copies',
	'ke09c94b1' => 'Written between 2022 and 2026 at a single café table in Da\'an District, Taipei, Small Hours gathers twenty-one essays across 248 pages. Clara Hsu records the subtle rhythm of early mornings, street vendors setting up their stalls, passing commuters, and the quiet transitions of weather. The book offers calm reflections on solitude, ordinary routines, and the gradual passage of time in a modern metropolis. Designed with a format of 14 × 21 cm, the volume is presented as an intentional physical object meant to be read slowly over quiet mornings.',
